## Summary

On mobile, when the Pocket/web page is backgrounded for even a short time and then brought back to the foreground, the client often sits in `disconnected` for up to ~10 seconds before it recovers. The reconnect machinery itself is fine — what's missing is an **eager reconnect when the page becomes visible again** (`visibilitychange`). This proposes a small, three-part addition to `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-connection`.

## Environment

- `@deepseek-ai/dsh` 0.1.5-rc.1 (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-connection` same version), web profile served from the published frontend bundle
- Android Chrome, page reached through a cloudflared tunnel
- Repro: open the web UI → wait for `connected` → background the tab ≥30s → foreground it → state shows `disconnected` and stays there for seconds before auto-recovery

## Root cause (verified against the published bundle)

`ConnectionController` (source region `lib/types/client/connection.js`):

- Exponential backoff reconnect: base 500ms, factor 2, capped at `backoffMaxMs=10000` — good, no change needed there.
- The **only** external wake-up signal is browser `online`/`offline` (`watchBrowserNetwork`, wired at the `provide("connection")` site).
- There is **no `visibilitychange` listener anywhere** in the client packages (0 grep hits).

Mobile browsers freeze background-tab timers and tear down long-lived connections (SSE/WS — more so through a tunnel). Typical timeline: while backgrounded, several reconnect attempts fail → backoff climbs to the 10s cap → the user returns and has to wait out the current backoff timer. The recovery loop is fine; it just never hears "the user is back".

## Proposed fix (minimal: one new signal, no redesign)

**1. `ConnectionController.refresh()`** — reuse the existing `reconnect()` (which already resets the attempt counter and does an immediate retry), but never tear down a healthy generation:

```ts
/** Foreground nudge: retry immediately, but never tear down a healthy generation. */
refresh() {
    if (!this.running) return;
    if (this.lastState === "connected") return;
    this.reconnect();
}
```

**2. `watchBrowserVisibility(controller)`** — next to `watchBrowserNetwork` (source region `lib/types/client/index.js`):

```ts
function watchBrowserVisibility(controller) {
    const browser = globalThis.window;
    const document = browser?.document;
    if (browser === void 0 || document === void 0 || typeof document.addEventListener !== "function") return () => {};
    const visible = () => {
        if (document.visibilityState !== "visible") return;
        if (browser.navigator?.onLine === false) return; // offline recovery belongs to the online event
        controller.refresh();
    };
    document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", visible);
    return () => {
        document.removeEventListener("visibilitychange", visible);
    };
}
```

**3. Wiring** — mount/dispose alongside the network watcher:

```ts
const releaseOwner = (current) => {
    if (owner !== current) return;
    owner = void 0;
    current.stopNetworkWatch();
    current.stopVisibilityWatch(); // new
    current.controller.stop();
    // ...
};
// in start():
const current = {
    token,
    source,
    controller,
    stopNetworkWatch: watchBrowserNetwork(controller),
    stopVisibilityWatch: watchBrowserVisibility(controller) // new
};
```

`ConnectionController` is exported, so `refresh()` needs a matching declaration in `lib/types/client/connection.d.ts`. `watchBrowserVisibility` stays module-internal.

## Design notes / alternatives considered

| Alternative | Why rejected |
|---|---|
| Unconditional `reconnect()` on visible | Every app switch would tear down a healthy connection → needless resync churn |
| Health-check RPC probe on foreground | Larger scope (new app-level channel); possible follow-up |
| Debounce | Foregrounding emits one `visible`; generation aborts are clean — no timer needed |
| UI-only fix | Cosmetic; connection still recovers slowly |

Edge case: if a stream died while backgrounded but the client still believes it is `connected`, `refresh()` is a no-op — but once JS resumes, the dead stream errors immediately, and with `attempt=0` the next retry lands within 250–500ms. The proposal targets the real slow path: backoff already at the cap when the user returns.

## Expected behavior after the fix

Foregrounding a non-connected client retries immediately (attempt reset), turning the worst-case ~10s `disconnected` wait into ~0. Healthy connections are untouched.

## Test sketch

Using the existing browser fixture machinery (`FixtureOptions`):

1. `visible` while `connected` → current generation is **not** aborted.
2. `visible` while `disconnected` (mid-backoff) → `onReconnectRequested` fires immediately, attempt counter resets.
3. `visible` with `navigator.onLine === false` → no reconnect (still waits for `online`).
4. `visible` after `stop()` → no-op, no throw.

## 环境

- macOS arm64,基于源码 `ddefc45fbc`(`0.1.6-alpha.2`)构建桌面端,使用 `apps/desktop` 打包脚本(未签名 `--dir` 模式)。

## 触发条件与时间线

普通更新 + 强制更新流程由 `63dd8fb80d`(*feat(desktop): add ordinary and mandatory update flows*,2026-09-16 合入,**晚于** `0.1.6-alpha.1`)引入。任何会打开这些对话框的路径都会触发本问题:

- 启动时的强制更新策略(mandatory policy)检查——当打包时烧入的策略要求认证时(例如从 `.env.macos` 带入的 `test` 部署策略);
- 点击应用菜单中的 **Check for Updates**(`openUpdatePrompt`);
- 服务端下发强制更新决策(策略码 `40005`)。

## 现象

一个全窗口的空白(白色)模态覆盖层挡住主窗口——应用呈现"白屏"且无法交互。主页面本身是健康的:通过 `--remote-debugging-port` 检查,`/json/list` 显示 `dsh-app://app/` 正常加载并工作,同时存在一个渲染为空的 `dsh-app://shell/update-dialog.html`(或 `.../mandatory-update.html`)页面。

## 根因

1. `apps/desktop/src/main.ts` 中的 `protocol.handle(SCHEME, ...)` 只服务 `url.hostname === 'app'` 的请求,**其余 hostname 一律返回 404**;
2. `63dd8fb80d` 引入的对话框加载 `dsh-app://shell/update-dialog.html` / `dsh-app://shell/mandatory-update.html`(见 `apps/desktop/src/update-dialog.ts`、`apps/desktop/src/mandatory-update-window.ts`),但协议处理器没有 hostname 为 `shell` 的路由,这些文档全部 404;
3. `createUpdateOverlay`(`apps/desktop/src/update-overlay.ts`)以父窗口完整内容尺寸创建对话框窗口,配置为 `frame: false`、`transparent: true`、`modal: true`,并在 `ready-to-show` 时显示。404 文档同样会触发 `ready-to-show`,因此**一个空的全窗口模态被显示出来**,阻塞整个应用(同时还会给父窗口插入模糊滤镜)。

值得注意的是,包含这些文档的 `renderer/` 目录**已经**被打包进产物(files 清单含 `renderer/**/*`),缺失的只是协议路由。

## 修复建议(已在本地验证)

为 `shell` hostname 服务打包内的 renderer 目录,与现有 `app` 分支同构:

```ts
// 在 protocol.handle(SCHEME, ...) 中,最终的 404 之前加入
if (url.hostname === 'shell') {
  return serveWebDocument(request, join(app.getAppPath(), 'renderer'))
}
```

加上该分支后对话框正常加载并工作(已在打包产物上验证:对话框正常渲染、按钮可用、关闭行为符合预期)。

## 为什么 CI 没有发现

CI 没有产出桌面端打包产物的任务,而 dev 模式与打包版共用同一个处理器——缺失的路由直到真实打包产物首次打开这些对话框时才会暴露。增加一个断言 `dsh-app://shell/update-dialog.html` 可解析的单元测试,或一个打包冒烟测试,即可覆盖此类问题。

# `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web` fails out-of-the-box — `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-rc.2` ships with incomplete `dependencies` and stale `dist-tags.latest`

## TL;DR

Running `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web` on a clean machine (Node 22) crashes during plugin load with two distinct packaging bugs in the published `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-rc.2` bundle:

1. **18 `@deepseek-ai/*` packages required at runtime are not declared as `dependencies`** (only as peer deps of internal sub-packages), so a fresh `npx` install never fetches them — `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` on `cordis-plugin-group`, `dsh-session-persistence`, `dsh-jobs`, `dsh-bash-local`, etc.
2. **Even after installing all 18 missing packages, the loader still fails** with `SyntaxError: The requested module '@deepseek-ai/dsh-session' does not provide an export named 'snapshotJsonValue'` — because the `latest` dist-tag of `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session` (and many siblings) is stuck at `0.0.1-rc.1` while `dsh@0.1.5-rc.2` was built against `0.1.5-rc.2`.

Both bugs are reproducible on a brand-new machine in under two minutes. The README's only documented install command (`npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web`) does not work.

## Environment

- macOS 15, Node `v22.22.0`, npm `10.9.8`
- `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-rc.2` (the version currently on the `latest` npm dist-tag)
- No prior install of any `@deepseek-ai/*` package (clean `npx` cache)

## Reproduction

```sh
npx --yes @deepseek-ai/dsh web
```

### Failure 1 — missing peer dependencies

```
node:internal/modules/package_json_reader:314
  throw new ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND(packageName, fileURLToPath(base), null);
        ^

Error [ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND]: Cannot find package '@deepseek-ai/cordis-plugin-group'
  imported from .../node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-app-boot/lib/index.js
```

`@deepseek-ai/dsh-app-boot@0.1.5-rc.2` declares `@deepseek-ai/cordis-plugin-group@^1.0.2` as a `peerDependency`, but the top-level `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-rc.2` package.json lists it under neither `dependencies` nor `peerDependencies` — only `cordis-plugin-hmr`, `cordis-plugin-include`, `cordis-plugin-loader`, `cordis-plugin-timer` are direct deps. Same pattern for 17 other packages that the loader needs but `dsh` never asks npm to fetch:

```
@deepseek-ai/dsh-anonymous-user-id
@deepseek-ai/dsh-attachment
@deepseek-ai/dsh-bash-local
@deepseek-ai/dsh-code-runtime
@deepseek-ai/dsh-compaction
@deepseek-ai/dsh-fs
@deepseek-ai/dsh-jobs
@deepseek-ai/dsh-output-retention
@deepseek-ai/dsh-sandbox
@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-persistence
@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-query
@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-telemetry
@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-title-llm
@deepseek-ai/dsh-settings
@deepseek-ai/dsh-shell
@deepseek-ai/dsh-spill
@deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent-in-process-driver
@deepseek-ai/dsh-util-time
```

### Failure 2 — API mismatch from stale `dist-tags.latest`

After installing every missing dep above (pinned to `0.1.5-rc.2`), the loader still fails:

```
Error: failed to import loader entry session-log-download
  (@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-log-export):
  The requested module '@deepseek-ai/dsh-session' does not provide
  an export named 'snapshotJsonValue'
```

Cause: `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session`'s npm `dist-tags.latest` is `0.0.1-rc.1`, which predates the `snapshotJsonValue` export. The version the rest of `dsh@0.1.5-rc.2` was built against (`0.1.5-rc.2`) only exists on `dist-tags.next` / `dist-tags.alpha`. Same staleness for `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-persistence`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-jobs`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-settings`, etc. — `npm install <name>` resolves to the old `latest` and silently picks an incompatible API surface.

## Working workaround (for anyone stuck)

```sh
mkdir dsh-fix && cd dsh-fix
npm init -y >/dev/null
npm install @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-rc.2
npm install \
    @deepseek-ai/cordis-plugin-group@1.0.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-anonymous-user-id@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-attachment@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-bash-local@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-code-runtime@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-compaction@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-fs@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-jobs@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-output-retention@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-sandbox@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-session-persistence@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-session-query@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-session-telemetry@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-session-title-llm@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-settings@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-shell@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-spill@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent-in-process-driver@0.1.5-rc.2 \
    @deepseek-ai/dsh-util-time@0.1.5-rc.2
./node_modules/.bin/dsh web
```

After that the server starts cleanly on `http://127.0.0.1:3080` and the token-URL flow works.

## Suggested fix

1. **Move all 18 (and likely a few more) `@deepseek-ai/*` peer-only packages from `peerDependencies` to `dependencies` in `apps/cli/package.json`.** They are hard runtime requirements, not "host-provided" peers. (`pnpm-lock.yaml` already records them as resolvable — `npx` just doesn't reach the transitive peers.)
2. **Republish the dist-tags.** Either (a) move every package to its current `next`/`alpha` release and re-point `latest`, or (b) republish `0.1.5-rc.2` across the whole tree so `latest` matches. Otherwise `npm install <pkg>@latest` will keep picking `0.0.1-rc.1`.
3. The release workflow (`scripts/release.sh` or equivalent) should either pin explicit versions in `apps/cli/package.json` or refuse to publish if `dist-tags.latest` lags behind the CLI's release commit.

## Notes

- The README states "Submit feedback or bug reports through GitHub Discussions" — filing here per that.
- A user could not have discovered this from the docs: the only documented install is `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web`, which currently fails. The dev path (`git clone` + `pnpm install`) is unaffected because pnpm resolves transitives through the workspace.
- Filed from a fresh macOS box; no global `dsh` install involved.

