## Observed result

`0.1.5-rc.3` — the click handler *runs*, and then absolutely nothing happens:

```text
RPC during click: []
pageerrors/warnings: []
```

`0.1.7-rc.2` — same script, same steps:

```text
RPC during click: ["200 http://127.0.0.1:3299/api/session/create"]
```

That the same flow works on `0.1.7-rc.2` also shows the host side is fine — session creation in a brand-new empty workspace succeeds there. It is purely the 0.1.5-rc.3 client.

## Root cause (0.1.5-rc.3)

`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace/lib/client.js`:

```js
// line 81
startSession(workspaceId) {
  const workspace = this.workspaces.list.getSnapshot();
  const sessions = this.sessions.list.getSnapshot();
  const current = sessions.current;
  const currentWorkspaceId = current === void 0 ? void 0
    : workspace.items.find((item) => item.sessionIds.includes(current))?.workspaceId;
  // line 86 — recent is gated on BOTH phases AND on the sessions store
  const recent = workspace.phase === "ready" && sessions.phase === "ready"
    ? recentWorkspace(workspace.items, sessions.byId) : void 0;
  const target = workspaceId ?? currentWorkspaceId ?? recent;
  if (target === void 0) {                 // line 88
    this.sessions.clear();                 // line 89  ← silently clears
    this.ctx.layout.selectPanel(null);     // line 90
    return;                                // line 91  ← no error, no RPC, no UI feedback
  }
  this.openWorkspace(target).catch((reason) => {
    console.warn("new session failed:", reason);   // line 94 — console only
  });
}
```

With **no sessions in the workspace at all**, `recentWorkspace(workspace.items, sessions.byId)` returns `undefined` and `currentWorkspaceId` cannot be derived either, so `target` is `undefined` and the function takes the silent `clear() + return` path. The sidebar button (`dsh-client-ui-sidebar/lib/client.js:262`) calls `startSession()` with **no argument**, so the one workspace id that *is* always known — the workspace the user just clicked from — never reaches this function.

Two aggravating factors:

1. The failure has no user-visible surface. Every error path here either returns silently or ends in `console.warn` (`new session failed:`), so a broken button is indistinguishable from a working one.
2. `recentWorkspace()` requires a current session, which is exactly what a new/empty workspace does not have.

## `0.1.7-rc.2` refactor (appears to fix it)

```js
async connectWorkspace(workspaceId) {           // line 787
  const workspace = this.workspaces.list.getSnapshot().items.find((item) => item.workspaceId === workspaceId);
  if (workspace === void 0) throw new Error(`uiWorkspace.connectWorkspace: unknown workspace ${workspaceId}`);
  const inflight = this.connecting.get(workspaceId);
  if (inflight !== void 0) return inflight;
  const attempt = this.reuseOrCreateBlank(workspace).finally(() => { this.connecting.delete(workspaceId); });
  this.connecting.set(workspaceId, attempt);
  return attempt;
}
reuseOrCreateBlank(workspace) {                 // line 798
  const archived = this.workspaces.list.getSnapshot().archivedSessionIds;
  const sessions = this.sessions.list.getSnapshot();
  for (const id of sessions.ids) {
    const summary = sessions.byId[id];
    if (summary === void 0 || !summary.blank || summary.cwd !== workspace.path
        || !workspace.sessionIds.includes(id) || archived.includes(id)) continue;
    return this.reuseBlank(workspace.workspaceId, id);
  }
  return this.sessions.create({ workspaceId: workspace.workspaceId });   // ← always has a target
